⸻

🌐 Why Patent #39 Matters

Deterministic Intelligence — unlike probabilistic AI — requires:
	•	strict lineage
	•	strict entropic bounds
	•	strict override governance
	•	strict replayable audit trails
	•	strict execution invariants

Patent #39 provides the missing container that binds these constraints into one reproducible OS-level envelope.

It fuses all prior machinery (#32–#36) into one deterministic execution shell.

This is the architecture-level leap needed to define DI as a true operating system, not merely a reasoning engine.

